# Copy where a spelled number happens to equal the size of one of this app's
# tables and is NOT about that table. One exact literal per line.
#
# tools/copy-count.mjs prints every line declared here on every run, so this
# file cannot grow quietly, and it FAILS when a declaration no longer matches
# anything — a line that has been reworded stopped having the reason it was
# allowed for.
#
# A stale count is never declarable. If the number is the size of a table, the
# copy asks the table.

# Four subsections of Title 14 section 7.40(b) were amended on 6 May 2026.
# That is a fact about the regulation, published by the department, and it does
# not move when a river is added to this app. It coincides with the river count
# and with the weir count, and means neither.
This reach is subsection 7.40(b)(4)(C), one of the four subsections amended on 6 May 2026. Before that amendment its text read "July 16 through December 31. No take or possession of Chinook Salmon." The amendment is what removed that sentence.
